@c src/frontend-forth/parser.texf — Forth Parser documentation fragment
@c Regenerate with: (regenerate-documentation-for-module "forth-parser")

@section FORTH Parser

The FORTH parser transforms tokenized Forth source code into an Abstract Syntax Tree (AST)
suitable for compilation to EIGHTBOL intermediate representation and assembly.

The parser:
@itemize @bullet
@item Converts Forth token streams to stack operation AST nodes
@item Manages word definitions (colon definitions) and constants
@item Handles control structures (IF/THEN/ELSE, BEGIN/UNTIL, loops)
@item Supports dialogue/narrative extensions (SAY, NARRATE, SHOW, etc.)
@item Generates appropriate AST nodes for stack, memory, and I/O operations
@end itemize

@subsection forth-parse-tokens

@deffn {Function} forth-parse-tokens TOKENS-PER-LINE
Parse tokenized Forth code into an AST.

@table @asis
@item Input @var{TOKENS-PER-LINE}
Output from @code{forth-tokenize-source}: list of token lists
@item Return value
@code{(:forth-program :definitions [...AST nodes...])}
@item Outputs
Top-level AST node containing all parsed definitions and statements
@end table

@subsection Behavior
Iterates through each line of tokens, calling @code{forth-parse-line} to generate
statements. Returns a complete Forth program node.

@end deffn

@subsection forth-parse-line

@deffn {Function} forth-parse-line CTX TOKENS
Parse a single line of tokens.

@table @asis
@item Input @var{CTX}
Parser context structure (tracks state, definitions)
@item Input @var{TOKENS}
List of tokens from one source line
@item Return value
(values statements-list tokens-consumed)
@item Statements
List of AST statement nodes generated from this line
@end table

@end deffn

@subsection forth-parse-token

@deffn {Function} forth-parse-token CTX TOKEN IDX TOKENS
Parse a single token within line context.

@table @asis
@item Input @var{CTX}
Parser context
@item Input @var{TOKEN}
Single token @code{(type . value)}
@item Input @var{IDX}
Token position in line
@item Input @var{TOKENS}
Full token list for lookahead
@item Return value
(values statement new-index) or (values nil new-index)
@item Statement
AST node or nil if no statement produced
@end table

@end deffn

@c AST Node Constructors
@section AST Node Constructors

@subsection make-forth-push-literal

@deffn {Function} make-forth-push-literal VALUE
Create a stack push for a literal value.

@table @asis
@item Input @var{VALUE}
Numeric or string literal
@item Return value
@code{(:forth-push-literal :value @var{VALUE})}
@end table

@end deffn

@subsection make-forth-push-identifier

@deffn {Function} make-forth-push-identifier NAME
Create a stack push for an identifier (variable fetch).

@table @asis
@item Input @var{NAME}
Variable or symbol name
@item Return value
@code{(:forth-push-identifier :name @var{NAME})}
@end table

@end deffn

@subsection make-forth-stack-op

@deffn {Function} forth-stack-op OP-NAME &key ARGS
Create a stack manipulation operation node.

@table @asis
@item Input @var{OP-NAME}
Operation symbol (e.g., @code{:DUP}, @code{:SWAP})
@item Keyword @var{ARGS}
Optional arguments list
@item Return value
@code{(:forth-stack-op :name @var{OP-NAME} :args @var{ARGS})}
@end table

@subsection Supported Operations
@table @code
@item :DUP
Duplicate top of stack
@item :SWAP
Exchange top two
@item :DROP
Remove top
@item :OVER
Copy second to top
@item :ROT
Rotate top three
@item :TWODUP, :TWOSWAP, :TWODROP
2-cell variants
@item :NIP, :TUCK
Additional manipulations
@item :ABS, :NEGATE
Unary arithmetic
@item :NOT, :ZEQUAL, :ZLT, :ZGT
Logical/comparison
@item :TORET, :FROMRET, :RATFETCH
Return stack ops
@item :PLUSSTORE, :CFETCH, :CSTORE
Memory operations
@item :SPACES, :PAGE
Output operations
@end table

@end deffn

@subsection make-forth-arithmetic

@deffn {Function} make-forth-arithmetic OP &key LEFT RIGHT RESULT-NAME
Create an arithmetic operation node.

@table @asis
@item Keyword @var{OP}
Operation: @code{:ADD}, @code{:SUB}, @code{:MUL}, @code{:DIV}, @code{:MOD}
@item Keyword @var{LEFT}
Left operand (optional)
@item Keyword @var{RIGHT}
Right operand (optional)
@item Keyword @var{RESULT-NAME}
Variable to store result (optional)
@item Return value
@code{(:forth-arithmetic :op @var{OP} :left @var{LEFT} :right @var{RIGHT} :result-name @var{RESULT-NAME})}
@end table

@subsection Bitwise Operations
@table @code
@item :AND, :OR, :XOR, :LSHIFT, :RSHIFT
Bitwise operations for integer manipulation
@end table

@end deffn

@subsection make-forth-comparison

@deffn {Function} make-forth-comparison OP &key LEFT RIGHT
Create a comparison operation node (for IF/THEN conditions).

@table @asis
@item Keyword @var{OP}
Comparison: @code{:EQ}, @code{:LT}, @code{:GT}, @code{:LE}, @code{:GE}, @code{:NE}
@item Keyword @var{LEFT}
Left operand
@item Keyword @var{RIGHT}
Right operand
@item Return value
@code{(:forth-comparison :op @var{OP} :left @var{LEFT} :right @var{RIGHT})}
@end table

@end deffn

@subsection make-forth-conditional

@deffn {Function} make-forth-conditional CONDITION THEN-BODY ELSE-BODY
Create a conditional (IF/THEN/ELSE) node.

@table @asis
@item Input @var{CONDITION}
Condition expression or AST node
@item Input @var{THEN-BODY}
List of statements to execute if true
@item Input @var{ELSE-BODY}
List of statements if false (may be empty)
@item Return value
@code{(:forth-conditional :condition @var{CONDITION} :then @var{THEN-BODY} :else @var{ELSE-BODY})}
@end table

@end deffn

@subsection make-forth-loop

@deffn {Function} make-forth-loop LOOP-TYPE INIT-BODY CONDITION-BODY BODY
Create a loop node.

@table @asis
@item Input @var{LOOP-TYPE}
@code{:begin-until}, @code{:begin-while}, or @code{:do-loop}
@item Input @var{INIT-BODY}
Initialization statements
@item Input @var{CONDITION-BODY}
Condition (for BEGIN/UNTIL or BEGIN/WHILE)
@item Input @var{BODY}
Loop body statements
@item Return value
@code{(:forth-loop :type @var{LOOP-TYPE} :init @var{INIT-BODY} :condition @var{CONDITION-BODY} :body @var{BODY})}
@end table

@end deffn

@c Output / Dialogue / Memory
@subsection Output and Dialogue Nodes

@deffn {Function} make-forth-print-value
Print top of stack value (Forth @code{.} word).

@table @asis
@item Return value
@code{(:forth-print-value)}
@end table

@end deffn

@deffn {Function} make-forth-print-string STRING
Print a string literal.

@table @asis
@item Input @var{STRING}
String to output
@item Return value
@code{(:forth-print-string :string @var{STRING})}
@end table

@end deffn

@deffn {Function} make-forth-print-char
Output character from top of stack (EMIT).

@table @asis
@item Return value
@code{(:forth-emit)}
@end table

@end deffn

@deffn {Function} make-forth-print-cr
Output carriage return / newline (CR).

@table @asis
@item Return value
@code{(:forth-print-cr)}
@end table

@end deffn

@deffn {Function} make-forth-input-key
Read a single key from input (KEY).

@table @asis
@item Return value
@code{(:forth-input-key)}
Pushes key code to stack
@end table

@end deffn

@deffn {Function} make-forth-input-line MAX-LENGTH
Read a line of input (ACCEPT).

@table @asis
@item Input @var{MAX-LENGTH}
Maximum input buffer size
@item Return value
@code{(:forth-input-line :max-length @var{MAX-LENGTH})}
Reads into buffer, pushes count
@end table

@end deffn

@deffn {Function} make-forth-dialogue DIALOGUE-TYPE &key SPEAKER TEXT OPTIONS
Create a dialogue/narrative node.

@table @asis
@item Input @var{DIALOGUE-TYPE}
@code{:say}, @code{:narrate}, @code{:choice}, @code{:show}, @code{:hide}, @code{:fade}, @code{:music}, @code{:sound}
@item Keyword @var{SPEAKER}
Speaker name (for dialogue)
@item Keyword @var{TEXT}
Text content
@item Keyword @var{OPTIONS}
Choice options (for @code{:choice})
@item Return value
@code{(:forth-dialogue :type @var{DIALOGUE-TYPE} :speaker @var{SPEAKER} :text @var{TEXT} :options @var{OPTIONS})}
@end table

@subsection Dialogue Extensions
@itemize @bullet
@item @code{:say} — Character dialogue
@item @code{:narrate} — Narrative text
@item @code{:choice} — Player choice menu
@item @code{:show}, @code{:hide} — Visual element toggling
@item @code{:fade} — Fade transition
@item @code{:music}, @code{:sound} — Audio playback
@end itemize

@end deffn

@subsection Memory and Definition Nodes

@deffn {Function} make-forth-variable-def NAME &optional INITIAL-VALUE
Create a variable definition node.

@table @asis
@item Input @var{NAME}
Variable name
@item Input @var{INITIAL-VALUE}
Initial value (optional)
@item Return value
@code{(:forth-variable :name @var{NAME} :initial-value @var{INITIAL-VALUE})}
@end table

@end deffn

@deffn {Function} make-forth-fetch ADDRESS
Create a memory fetch node (@).

@table @asis
@item Input @var{ADDRESS}
Address expression (TOS)
@item Return value
@code{(:forth-fetch :address @var{ADDRESS})}
@end table

@end deffn

@deffn {Function} make-forth-store ADDRESS VALUE
Create a memory store node (!).

@table @asis
@item Input @var{ADDRESS}
Address expression
@item Input @var{VALUE}
Value to store
@item Return value
@code{(:forth-store :address @var{ADDRESS} :value @var{VALUE})}
@end table

@end deffn

@deffn {Function} make-forth-word-def NAME PARAMS BODY
Create a colon definition node.

@table @asis
@item Input @var{NAME}
Word name
@item Input @var{PARAMS}
Parameter list (optional)
@item Input @var{BODY}
Body token list or AST nodes
@item Return value
@code{(:forth-word-def :name @var{NAME} :params @var{PARAMS} :body @var{BODY})}
@end table

@end deffn

@deffn {Function} make-forth-constant-def NAME VALUE
Create a constant definition node.

@table @asis
@item Input @var{NAME}
Constant name
@item Input @var{VALUE}
Constant value
@item Return value
@code{(:forth-constant :name @var{NAME} :value @var{VALUE})}
@end table

@end deffn

@subsection High-Level Interfaces

@deffn {Function} forth-compile-source SOURCE-STRING
Compile Forth source code string to AST.

@table @asis
@item Input @var{SOURCE-STRING}
Forth program text
@item Return value
@code{(:forth-program :definitions [...AST nodes...])}
@item Errors
Parse errors or invalid syntax
@end table

@end deffn

@deffn {Function} forth-compile-file FILENAME
Compile a .forth file to AST.

@table @asis
@item Input @var{FILENAME}
Path to .forth source file
@item Return value
@code{(:forth-program :definitions [...])}
@item Errors
File not found or parse errors
@end table

@end deffn

@subsection Typical Workflow
@enumerate
@item Call @code{forth-tokenize-source} to tokenize Forth source
@item Call @code{forth-parse-tokens} to produce AST
@item Walk AST and emit EIGHTBOL IR or assembly
@end enumerate

